  "body": "### Reproduction steps\n\nThe following works just fine in vscode.\n\n1. Re-open vscode devcontainer in zed\n2. Make sure docker in docker feature is installed\n3. Verify .docker/config.json looks like:\n```json\n{\n\t\"auths\": {\n\t\t\"ghcr.io\": {}\n\t},\n\t\"credsStore\": \"dev-containers-3d27e5b7-9adb-4407-a042-54dea14a26ed\"\n}\n```\n4. Run `docker login ghcr.io -u [USER] -p ghp_[YOURGITHUBTOKEN]`. Observe it fails with:\n\nWARNING! Using --password via the CLI is insecure. Use --password-stdin.\nerror saving credentials: error storing credentials - err: exit status 255, out: ``\n\n5. Edit ~/.docker/config.json to look like this:\n```json\n{\n        \"auths\": {\n                \"ghcr.io\": {}\n        },\n        \"credStore\": \"dev-containers-3d27e5b7-9adb-4407-a042-54dea14a26ed\"\n}\n```\n\nNote the credStore instead of credsStore.\n\n6. Run `docker login ghcr.io -u [USER] -p ghp_[YOURGITHUBTOKEN]`. Observe it succeeds.\n\n### Current vs. Expected behavior\n\nThe above works in vscode, but fails in zed. \n\n### Zed version and system specs\n\nZed: v0.228.0+stable.203.8421009ef8a022df1196d54bb42fd94366ec0988 (Zed) \nOS: macOS 26.3.1 (a) (Build 25D771280a)\nMemory: 64 GiB\nArchitecture: aarch64\n\nOrbStack Version 2.0.5 (19905)\n\n### Attach Zed log file\n\nnot applicable\n\n### Relevant Zed settings\n\nnot applicable\n\n### Relevant Keymap\n\nnot applicable\n\n### (for AI issues) Model provider details\n\nnot applicable\n\n### If you are using WSL on Windows, what flavor of Linux are you using?\n\nNone",
